      "notes": "18 statements in one chain, verified on CN03480580 2026-08-07 — 18 fields returned, no error. Replaces asking marker_states and all_marker_settings separately: status and values always arrive together, so the Active boxes can never disagree with the X and Y beside them."
    },
    "Get_Averaging": {
      "scpi": ":SENSe:AVERage:TRACe<trace_number>:COUNt?",
      "scpiFast": ":SENS:AVER:TRAC<trace_number>:COUN?",
      "description": "Trace averaging count.",
      "subsystem": "Trace",
      "returns": {
        "count": 1,
        "type": "NR1"
      },
      "notes": "The trace index sits in the MIDDLE: ':SENSe:AVERage:TRACe<n>:COUNt'. Eight spellings with it elsewhere — :TRACe:AVERage:COUNt, :SENSe:AVERage:COUNt, :AVERage:COUNt, :TRACe1:AVERage:COUNt and friends — all return -171 'Invalid expression', which is what made this look unsupported. Verified on CN03480580 2026-08-07: set 25 -> reads +25, set 100 -> reads +100."
    }
